>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must not be bool to avoid hardtanh bool error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor must not be complex to avoid clamp complex error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 3 (valid tensor shape: all dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (inplace flag is explicitly a boolean literal)
{v_2 : bool} |= v_2 = true ∨ v_2 = false
